GAL16V8
Partial VPA passthrough (for autovectored interrupts) from motherboard to external CPU & async DTACK generator (to external CPU) to replace 6800 bus accesses. CLK is the motherboard 8MHz line.

CLK FC0  FC1  VPAmb AS   P6   P7       P8    P9       GND
OE  P12  P13  P14   P15  P16  VPAext   DTACKext VMAmb VCC

; VPAext is purely combinational.
; Original equation: VPAext = NOT( NOT VPAmb AND FC1 AND FC0 )
; VPA to the external CPU should only be passed if an interrupt acknowledge cycle (ie. FC0 and FC1 are high)
VPAext = VPAmb + /FC1 + /FC0

; VMA is VPA delayed by one 8MHz clock cycle.
; The '.R' operator denotes a registered (clocked) output.
; Activate VMA to the motherboard on the first positive edge of the E clock after receiving a VPA signal.
; No harm to activate VMA even if it's an interrupt acknowledge cycle. This wouldn't happen usually, however.
VMAmb.R = VPAmb + AS

; DTACK is VPA delayed by two clock cycles.
; Chaining the registers like this achieves the two-cycle delay
; Time DTACK such that the external 68000 can latch data from the ACIAs when they are driving the bus for what they perceive to be a normal synchronous 6800 cycle.
DTACKext.R = VMAmb + AS

